  m_Name: M.O.C.K
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  projectName: 'M.O.C.K '
  description: "Menacing Omnicritical Contraption Kernel\nA critical art project
    wrapping a pointed game design argument in a joke. Built around the concept of
    the \"unbeatable machine,\" M.O.C.K. is a useless box game that confronts the
    player with the illusion of choice \u2014 inspired by the Mass Effect Andromeda
    controversy, where every ending amounted to the same differently-colored explosion.
    \nThe humor is intentional, as the absurd Team Fortress 2 audio brings it home.
    The buttons are supposed to represent YES/NO answering to the question \"Disam
    Bomb?\"\nBuilt and programmed in Arduino by me. I had to implement feedback when
    players hit buttons in the wrong order, since it would otherwise confuse them.
    Due to the limitations of a physical/Arduino product, it was not possible to
    adress it similarily, when players spammed buttons. It generated some good laughs!\n"
